cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below and credit the source editions named in README.md."
type: dataset
title: "Open Edda: a parallel Old Norse – Icelandic – English dataset of Snorri's Edda and the Poetic Edda"
abstract: >-
  Snorri Sturluson's Edda (Formáli, Gylfaginning, Skáldskaparmál, Háttatal) aligned paragraph by paragraph
  into 1,514 rows: Guðni Jónsson's normalised Old Norse (1954, via heimskringla.no), modern Icelandic spelling
  (Netútgáfan 1997 for Gylfaginning, automatic modernisation elsewhere) and English (A. G. Brodeur 1916;
  AI draft for Háttatal, unreviewed), with community overlays, cell statuses and openly licensed image
  records. The 45 poems of the Poetic Edda are aligned stanza by stanza (Guðni Jónsson 1949; H. A. Bellows
  1923 for 36 of them, B. Thorpe 1866 for two, AI drafts marked for the rest) into 1,952 rows and linked to
  Snorri's quotations of them. Further English versions (R. B. Anderson 1880, Thorpe 1866, a modernised
  English), a names index keyed to Wikidata and a reader's guide are included.
authors:
  - family-names: Sapunov
    given-names: Grigory
    email: grigory.sapunov@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-18"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://openedda.is"
repository-code: "https://github.com/parallel-classics/edda-data"
keywords:
  - Snorra Edda
  - Poetic Edda
  - Prose Edda
  - Old Norse
  - Icelandic
  - parallel corpus
  - digital edition
